  "notes": [
    "These are authored IDs, not a supported Archify event API.",
    "The two Kong nodes combine authentication and authorization in ONE DP; correlate their runtime phases separately.",
    "Customer ingress paths are illustrative proposals, not deployed configuration. Both target one backend.",
    "Entra DS synchronization is setup-time context, not an API request event; tenant identity is not implied.",
    "Do not infer IdP failure or backend non-arrival from a browser timeout.",
    "Revision 3 restores one shared test-ui node, g1-entry/g2-entry and adds g1-callback/g2-callback.",
    "g1-login/g2-login and callbacks represent front-channel redirects THROUGH THE SEPARATE BROWSER WINDOW, not direct IdP-to-Kong server callbacks.",
